Create a detailed dry media drawing of a butterfly resting on a wooden branch. Use graphite pencils and silverpoint for most of the artwork to draw fine lines, delicate wing veins, and subtle textures. Use charcoal only in small amounts around the background to build subtle contrast and create a clear emphasis on the central butterfly. Apply simple techniques like cross-hatching and smooth layering to add realistic texture to the wood and wings. At last, use a kneaded eraser to lift away pencil marks, creating bright, clean highlights along the edges of the wings.
